<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>🌡️ LIVE WATER TEMPERATURE</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/water_temperature/legend.png" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Surface water temperature (°F): cold <b>51°F</b> (deep blue) → <b>59°F</b> → warm <b>67°F</b> (red). Lakewide mean this run: <b>59.2°F</b>. White halo numbers are actual °F at that spot. The bar ends are recomputed every run from that day's water (1st/99th percentiles, clamped 32–86°F): blue always means the coldest water present and red the warmest, but the same color can stand for a different °F on different days — only the printed numbers are absolute.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/GLERL CoastWatch GLSEA (Great Lakes Surface Environmental Analysis)).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of wave and ice layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>🌡️ LIVE WATER TEMPERATURE — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/Great_Lakes_Live_Water_Temperature.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>21600</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
